From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrew Youll <adyoull@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 19:45:54 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] RISC OS: log stalls

A player reported the game stopping completely for 2-3 seconds every
10-20 minutes. With a log (fheroes2$Log), the game now records when it
stops for more than half a second, and why as far as it can tell:

- it ran without checking for events, so nothing else on the desktop
  could run either (with the step in progress: saving the autosave,
  starting a music track, a computer player's turn, the new day);
- checking for events (Wimp_Poll) took long: the desktop or another
  program held the computer;
- a wait took much longer than asked;
- one of those named steps took more than 300 ms.

Each line has the size of the heap (the "fheroes2 Heap" dynamic areas),
which is also added to the drawing times logged every 10 seconds.
